NAME: Weekly leaderboard
OWNER: Sales Manager
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Monday at 8:07 AM
MILESTONE: 2
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/spike-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Weekly leaderboard" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "Weekly leaderboard: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/spike-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.

Use the eod-parsing skill, section "Weekly". From /workspace/spike-team/data/eod/ build last week's and month-to-date leaderboards for closers and setters, mark each rep on track, yellow or behind against /workspace/spike-team/context/kpi-targets.md with two lines of why for each yellow or red, and pick one recommended conversation. If kpi-targets.md is missing, show the leaderboards and ask Dan for targets instead of guessing. Send it to Dan only. Save it to /workspace/spike-team/vault/Sales/Weekly/<monday>.md.
